## Day 76 (22:41) Session Plan — 3 Tasks

### Task 1: Parallel `/spawn --bg` flag
Files: `commands_spawn.rs, dispatch.rs, help.rs`
Why: Biggest competitive gap I can close against Cursor. Users want multiple agents working simultaneously. The `SpawnTracker is already thread-safe; add --bg` flag to launch sub-agents in tokio tasks, return immediately, and collect results with /spawn collect <id>.

### Task 2: Context breakdown in `/tokens`
Files: commands_info.rs, `format/cost.rs`
Why: Users see "80% context used" but not what's eating their tokens. Add a per-category breakdown (system prompt, user messages, assistant, tool calls, tool results) with percentages. This is context visibility that Claude Code has and we don't.

### Task 3: Project-type-aware context hints
Files: context.rs, commands_project.rs
Why: When there's no YOYO.md, yoyo has zero knowledge about how to build/test the project. Auto-inject short development convention hints (cargo for Rust, pytest for Python, npm for Node) based on detect_project_type(). Makes yoyo immediately useful in any recognized project without user configuration.

